-- a report weakened along an implication of warrants: the same molecule and the same number, resting on
-- less. This is the field's own identification scale, which it wrote down because identity is contested
-- in mass spectrometry: an MSI Level 1 identification rests on a comparison with an in-house standard, a
-- Level 2 annotation on a high-quality match to a spectral library, and the first implies the second.
-- The scale is a family of warrant types and the levels are maps between them; what the record stores is
-- the level as a label beside the number instead of the warrant it names.
rep-weaken : (W : Type 0) → (r : Report Nat) → (rep-warrant Nat r → W) → Report Nat
rep-weaken W r f = ( rep-mol Nat r , W , f (rep-witness Nat r) , rep-value Nat r )
